# TODO - CUDA Linux runtime and hermetic toolchain

## Objective

Port the exact CUDA runtime and repository-local development toolchains to Linux
while preserving platform-specific ABI loading, exact package identity, CPU
fallback, verifier authority, and existing Windows support.

## Acceptance

- Windows selects `ctypes.WinDLL`, `nvcuda.dll`, and its versioned NVRTC `.dll`;
  Linux selects `ctypes.CDLL`, `libcuda.so.1`, and a manifest-selected versioned
  NVRTC `.so` through one reviewed platform loader contract.
- Generic CUDA execution logic contains no hardcoded `13.3.1` toolkit path or
  Windows library suffix; the selected platform manifest owns release and
  library
  identity.
- Windows and Linux manifests pin platform, release, package versions, archive
  paths, sizes, toolkit roots, and SHA-256 values without a "latest" fallback.
- Shared Rust, Jig, LLVM, Python, and validation configuration no longer assumes
  a
  Windows target or `Scripts/*.exe/*.cmd` path on Linux.
- Linux missing-driver, missing-library, platform-mismatch, cleanup, and CPU
  fallback routes fail explicitly without changing semantic acceptance.
- Linux x86-64 exact CPU/CUDA differential tests and retained live-device
  evidence
  exist for every support or performance claim, while existing Windows gates
  pass.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder or undocumented
  workaround
  required for the objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove
  the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

